  "full": {
   "text": "THE FAMILY GOES CAMPING IN THE WOODS. THEY PACK THEIR TRAILER AND SET OUT IN THE MORNING. THEY HIKING THROUGH THE FOREST, LISTENING TO THE SOUNDS OF THE WOODS. THE SUN RISES AND THE SKY BECOMES BLUE. THEY SET UP THEIR CAMPING SITE AND MAKE THEIR BEDS. THEY EAT MEALS IN THE PINE TREE AND SLEEP UNDER THE STARLIGHT. THE WOODS ARE QUIET AND CALM. THEY RELAX AND RELAY ON EACH OTHER. THEY SHARE STORIES AND SMILE. THE NIGHT IS QUIET AND THE WOODS ARE THEIR FRIENDS. THEY WAKE UP IN THE MORNING AND LOOK UP AT THE SKY. THEY ARE HAPPY AND CONTENT. THEY RETURN HOME WITH A MEMORABLE EXPERIENCE IN THE WOODS. P.S. THE FAMILY EXPERIENCED ADVENTURE IN THE WOODS. THEY FELT THE ENERGY OF THE WOODS AND THE SENSE OF EXPLORATION. THE FIRE WAS A SYMBOL OF TOGETHERSHIP AND COOLING DOWN AFTER A LONG DAY.",
